  "THE SENSITIVE-DIFF CLASSIFIER IS A REGEX AND IT MISSED THE ONLY REAL WIDENING (adversary, run-adversary-d8, the second time the merge gate was used in anger). scripts/merge_builder.py:96-98 matches allowlist|_guard_|approver|GUARD_VERSION|autopolicy|/approve|confirm. On builder-d8 it flagged six lines that were the benign new read-only endpoint, and MISSED _real_broker() -> _broker_is_real() at the two /fund/venue/backfill guards - which flipped one of eight flag combinations from refuse to allow on the live .env, on an endpoint that appends ORDER_FILLED to the real ledger (backfill.py:230). The vocabulary has no term for backfill, for ledger-write endpoints, or for guard-predicate renames. A KEYWORD FILTER IS STANDING IN FOR A CONTROL-FLOW QUESTION. Adversary recommendation, adopted: flag any changed line that alters a boolean used in a raise HTTPException refusal, independent of vocabulary. Suggested additions regardless: any diff touching a function whose result gates a raise/refuse; any change to a predicate named *_is_*/_real_*/_allowed_*; any file that appends EventType.ORDER_* . This is a defect in the fund own instrument, found by using it.",
