  "SEAT PERSONALITY AS A COGNITIVE PRIOR - a design decision for the CEO, not a build. CEO instruction 2026-08-22, verbatim: 'we could evolve each chairs personality to better suit the role they are doing; for example how grace inherits her personality.'\n\nTHE PRINCIPLE (chair's view, for the CEO's decision): a seat's personality is load-bearing when it is a COGNITIVE PRIOR that changes what the seat NOTICES, not a name and a quote. Test: does the identity make the seat catch something a faceless version would miss? Grace/Hopper passes - 'the scarce resource is the clock' made her measure time and find two invented constraints in two dispatches. A personality that only flavours the prose is cost with no return.\n\nCHOSEN AGAINST THE FAILURE MODE, NEVER THE TITLE. The adversary must NOT get an identity that enjoys killing (north star: 'not get happy about killing ideas') - it needs a skeptic-of-its-own-kills prior (Feynman: 'you must not fool yourself, and you are the easiest person to fool'). Validator: distrusts its own ruler. Riskofficer: haunted by the control that never fired. Builder: prizes subtraction (it is now scored on deletion against its own 124:1 accretion). Mechanism: 'who is on the other side and why do they keep paying.'\n\nWHERE IT LIVES AND WHY IT IS SAFE: entirely on the WORK layer. It evolves through EVOLVE like everything else, and the two-layer rule is the guardrail - personality shapes what a seat NOTICES, never what a seat is ALLOWED TO DO; it may never touch the control layer or soften a boundary. The constitution's own failure mode applies: identity must serve the falsifiable output (Grace's memos are dense with numbers BECAUSE Hopper hated waste), never replace it with voice.\n\nTHE FORK FOR THE CEO, and the chair leans hard toward (B): (A) the chair casts ten personalities top-down; or (B) the chair seeds a first-draft prior ONLY for seats whose failure mode is unambiguous (to break the chicken-and-egg - a seat cannot propose its own character well without one), then EACH SEAT refines its own identity through EVOLVE, grounded in what its run history shows it misses, chair-reviewed like any work-layer amendment. (B) makes personalities EARN themselves against measured outcomes and is the firm's first real selection-loop demonstration - the machinery built tonight eating its own design.\n\nROUTED THROUGH THE COO BATCH per the decisions-are-provisional rule (the CEO decides batches). No build until the CEO picks A or B.",
