  "THE FIDELITY LEDGER - extend vs_assumption from cost to everything else the backtest predicted. CEO 2026-08-22: 'A fidelity ledger. yes and i think parts of it already exists.' HE IS RIGHT AND I UNDERSTATED IT. GET /fund/tca already carries vs_assumption - assumed_bps_per_side 5.0 against realised 5.56, excess 0.56, sample 8 - which IS predicted-versus-realised, already built and already the right shape. It just only covers COST. THE BUILD IS AN EXTENSION, NOT A NEW SYSTEM. Reuse that exact pattern for the other quantities a backtest predicts and a live run can contradict: TURNOVER (backtest daily_turnover_pct against realised from fills); EXPOSURE (predicted average and peak against realised from the book); DRAWDOWN PATH (the backtest max drawdown and its shape against live); and EXIT TIMING (a rule's predicted trigger date against the date it actually fired - four dated exits exist and rules carry on_date, so this one is directly checkable today). WHY THIS IS THE HIGHEST-VALUE REPORTING WORK IN THE FUND: at $2,000 you CANNOT prove returns. A decent year is $283, and the gate's own power is 22.8 percent at Sharpe 1.0 - separating edge from luck takes years we do not have. What you CAN prove in weeks is FIDELITY: that the machine does what it says and reality matched the model. The CEO's stated goal is proving we can manage $2k well enough to justify $10k, and a ledger showing three months where realised tracked predicted, the controls fired when they should have, and we know what a fill costs is a far stronger argument for capital than any P&L this account can produce. RETURNS DO NOT TRANSFER AT THIS SIZE. BEHAVIOUR DOES. THE FRAMING THAT MAKES THE NUMBER HONEST: do not ask 'did we return 15 percent'. Ask 'WAS THE REALISED OUTCOME INSIDE THE BACKTEST'S PREDICTED DISTRIBUTION'. That is a weaker claim and it is actually testable with few observations, which is the whole point at this size. DESIGN IT NOW EVEN THOUGH NOTHING IS DEPLOYED - that is deliberate. An instrument designed after the fact measures whatever happened to be easy to capture. Design against what the backtest ALREADY emits, so the comparison is possible on the FIRST deployed strategy rather than the third. ABSENCE DISCIPLINE, non-negotiable: a dimension the backtest did not predict renders UNPREDICTED, and a live run without enough observations renders INSUFFICIENT. Neither is ever zero and neither is ever a pass. This fund found four instruments in one day that answer could-not-measure with zero.",
