  "DISPATCH READY - fire on the next free slot. CEO instruction 2026-08-21: run the mechanism with what we learned today. WHY THIS SEAT, NOW: the firm measured its own throughput today and leg 2 of the team metric - candidates reaching the belt per week, target 3-5 - is running at roughly ONE. Every learning of the last two days made the pipeline STRICTER and none of them generated a candidate. The mechanism is the only seat whose output is candidates. That is the gap the CEO named. FOUR THINGS LEARNED TODAY THAT CHANGE WHAT A GOOD PROPOSAL LOOKS LIKE - all four are already written into mechanism.md as chair notes, read them there in full: (1) capacity is bounded by your LEAST capacious leg, and the belt currently computes it with an unseeded hash tie-break that swung one candidate 16.7x - so name the leg you believe binds rather than leaning on capacity_usd; (2) a belt run covered window follows the wall clock, so NO prior belt result is a baseline for a new one; (3) the 37 pre-instrument candidates are FENCED full stop - not citable as we already tried something like this; (4) the gate has never passed a genuine candidate, so a proposal whose case is it should pass the gate is making an unevidenced claim - state what would make it FAIL. THE MATERIAL YOU HAVE, and it is real rather than speculative: the analyst delivered entry-14 groundwork with the population MEASURED - 537 424B filings, ~99 clean follow-on equity placements over 5.6 years (~18/yr), discount median -3.18 pct / mean -5.48 pct / t=-3.44 on n=24, matching published literature - and the analyst own conclusion that THE EDGE IS NOT OURS TO COLLECT because the discount compensates the ALLOCATED placement buyer and the secondary drift is nil at |t| <= 0.66. Treat that as a measured wall, not an invitation to re-litigate it. Also dead and not to be revived without new data: 8-K item 5.02 officer-departure drift (calendar-time t=0.65, beta_IWM 0.96, alpha t=-0.42 - the basket IS the small-cap index). WHAT I WANT: proposals with a named counterparty and a claim type, as always - and given the premia sleeve holds $917.05 live with NO criterion since 2026-08-19, a PREMIA claim that can be judged without waiting for gate v5 is worth more to this firm right now than an alpha claim that cannot be judged at all. Do not propose a parameter sweep. Do not propose anything requiring a cross-sectional sort on price level, market cap, dollar volume or share count - our price feed carries a verified ~44 pct/yr phantom factor and the gate is structurally blind to it.",
