  "AMENDS 0ffa4aee - MOCK MODE IS ISOLATED, NOT EPHEMERAL. It persists to Postgres like everything else. CEO instruction 2026-08-21, verbatim: \"but lest make sure our tests persist on a postgres table basically a replica so we can persist it.\" THIS NAMES THE ORIGINAL SIN BETTER THAN THE EARLIER TICKET DID. USE_FAKE_FIRESTORE was not wrong because it isolated test work from the real ledger - isolation is correct and 0ffa4aee keeps it. It was wrong because it isolated by making things EPHEMERAL: an in-memory store that threw the record away. That is how 552 events (seq 161-712) came to live on one disk while the status endpoint reported successful mirroring hourly, and it is why the CEO said earlier, verbatim, \"no more of fake firestore, everything is served off postgres and persistent\" and \"I think we should make agent interactions also durable on postgres so they are durable and retrievable on demand.\" ISOLATION AND DURABILITY ARE ORTHOGONAL. The old flag treated them as one thing. They are not: the requirement is a SEPARATE ledger, not a DISPOSABLE one. THE AMENDMENT: mock mode writes to a persistent Postgres store - krypton_fund_test already exists on the same instance at 127.0.0.1:5433, or an equivalently durable table if you judge a separate database wrong. Same schema, same durability guarantees, same append-only discipline, same fold code. What differs is WHICH store, and nothing else. WHY THIS IS WORTH MORE THAN TIDINESS, and it is the CEO forward-looking half: a persistent mock ledger makes test runs a RECORD rather than an exhaust. You can ask what a test did last week, diff two runs of the same strategy, and - directly relevant to the stress tests against past market events he named - compare a replay of 2020-03 run today against the same replay run after a harness change. AN EPHEMERAL MOCK LEDGER MAKES THE REPLAY ENGINE MEASURE NOTHING TWICE. The whole value of replaying history is the comparison, and a comparison needs both runs to still exist. CONSEQUENCES TO GET RIGHT: (a) the mock store is append-only and event-sourced exactly like the fund store - do not build a lighter-weight variant, because a second event model is a second place for the fold to disagree; (b) NAV and the book fold from whichever store the mode selects, with the mode stamped on the answer, so a mock NAV can never be read as the fund NAV; (c) durability monitoring covers BOTH stores - the failure we are guarding against is precisely a store that reports success while persisting nothing; (d) the two stores must never be joined or unioned in any reader.",
  // 2695 chars — longest
  "DESIGN THE MEASUREMENT TRADING PROGRAMME - trades whose purpose is a number, not a profit. CEO brainstorm decision 2026-08-22: agreed on trades-as-paid-experiments, and separately asked of the unmeasured cost model \"why not fix this\". THESE ARE THE SAME PROJECT and that is the point of this dispatch. CHAIR CORRECTION FIRST, because the brief must not repeat my own overstatement: the cost model is NOT unmeasured. GET /fund/tca already separates informative from uninformative fills by venue (alpaca 10 counted, paper 10 excluded), splits delay from execution, tracks approval latency, and carries vs_assumption: assumed_bps_per_side 5.0, REALISED 5.56, excess 0.56, SAMPLE 8. The machinery is good. THE GAP IS SAMPLE SIZE, and those 8 fills are all from 2026-08-13/14 - the pre-paper era, before the connector was routing anywhere real. So the fix is not to build a cost model. It is to FEED the one we have. WHAT I WANT FROM THIS SEAT: design a programme of deliberately small trades whose PURPOSE IS MEASUREMENT, not profit. The CEO already authorised experimental deployments on exactly this basis (constitution, 2026-08-21): explicit learning goal written down, alpaca venue, exit rules committed before entry, notional capped, CEO click per deploy. This extends it from one-off to a programme. DESIGN QUESTIONS THAT ARE YOURS: how many fills does the cost model need before its number is trustworthy - state the target and your basis for it, since n=8 with a 0.56bp excess is not obviously enough to charge a backtest with. Which liquidity tiers must be sampled, and why those - a cost model calibrated only on SPY tells us nothing about what a thin name costs us, and our universe is 201 small and mid caps. What notional per trade balances informativeness against tuition. And what the STOPPING rule is: this programme ends when the number is trustworthy, not when someone forgets about it. THE HONEST FRAMING TO KEEP: the loss is tuition and it is budgeted. A trade in this programme is not expected to make money and must never be scored as though it were - if any of these ends up in a P&L attribution as a failed strategy, the programme has been misrecorded. SEQUENCING CONSTRAINT, do not skip it: R23 gates this. tca.py:212 must prefer the SUBMITTED leg over the self-declared fill label before the programme starts, or we will spend real money generating fills whose venue label may lie - which is exactly how the first experimental deployment produced ZERO cost information while wearing an alpaca label. Measure nothing until the reader is honest. Also note the fund now runs autopolicy v4 and the mode work is in flight; coordinate with alpaca-paper being the deployment mode.",
  // 2777 chars — longest
  "KILL USE_FAKE_FIRESTORE ENTIRELY, AND MAKE EVERY ORDER ROUTE TO ALPACA OR FAIL - NO SILENT SIMULATOR. CEO instruction 2026-08-21, verbatim: \"every order needs to route to alpaca paper account no sham and kill fake_firestore; I do not want it biting us no more\" - and separately, on the flag itself: \"FAKE FIRESTORE was a workaround when firestore got rate limited and postgres was not in; as previously noted is an artifact - hopefully all of it is gone now.\" IT IS NOT GONE. Five live references: fund.py:129 (_mock_mode) and firebase.py:42, :66, :81, :84. PART A - THE SHAM, and this is the sharper half. The connector ternary at fund.py:151-163 has THREE ways to reach PaperConnector and TWO OF THEM ARE SILENT: (1) FUND_REAL_BROKER=1 -> Alpaca, fine; (2) _mock_mode() true -> paper, gated on USE_FAKE_FIRESTORE; (3) ALPACA_API_KEY present -> Alpaca; (4) ELSE -> PaperConnector, SILENTLY. That last branch is the sham the CEO means: if the key is ever absent, typo-d, or dropped by a restart that does not carry the environment, orders go to a SIMULATOR and the book moves as though they were real - with no error, no log line, and no way to tell from the outside. THE FIX: remove the silent fallback. If Alpaca is not configured, the fund must FAIL CLOSED - refuse to construct an order path at all, loudly, at startup - rather than quietly simulate. A fund that cannot reach its broker must know it cannot reach its broker. Keep PaperConnector as a class if tests need it; what must die is a PRODUCTION PATH that reaches it by omission. PART B - remove USE_FAKE_FIRESTORE from app/ and scripts/ entirely, and from .env. Note firebase.py:81-87 currently uses it as a SAFETY interlock (refusing to open a real Firestore client while the flag is set) - that interlock is protecting against a mode that will no longer exist, so remove the mode and the interlock together rather than leaving a guard for a state that cannot occur. PART C, same class, found today the hard way: events.store_backend() at events.py:218 defaults to \"firestore\" when FUND_STORE is unset. A spine restart that did not carry the shell variable silently moved the whole fund off Postgres; it was caught only by a 503 on a desk write. The chair has written FUND_STORE=postgres into .env as an immediate mitigation, but THE DEFAULT ITSELF IS THE DEFECT - a default that relocates the ledger is a trapdoor. Make it fail closed or default to postgres, and say which you chose and why. EVIDENCE THIS ALREADY COST US: the flag flip on 2026-08-21 moved order execution from paper to a real Alpaca account as a side effect of a DURABILITY fix, and fund.py:132-140 carries a docstring saying _real_broker() exists precisely to prevent that conflation. Supersedes and folds in the earlier 09e49ae5 and b72847bc.",
