  "OPEN THE UNIVERSE - the upper ADV cut is a constraint designed for a fund we are not. CEO instruction 2026-08-22, verbatim: \"one more thing we are not limited to any mid-cap or small-cap; everything is fair play and we have fractional shares; goal is how can we use our agentic infra for yields that dwarfs human teams.\" WHAT IS ACTUALLY THERE, traced rather than assumed: the hunting ground reports adv_band_usd [500000, 250000000] and count 200, and universe.py:218-219 shows the band is DERIVED, not chosen - adv_lo = min_capacity * turnover / participation, adv_hi = max_capacity * turnover / participation. So the upper cut exists because a max_capacity parameter says do not research names where our capacity would exceed some figure. THAT IS A SCALE CONSTRAINT AND AT $2,000 NAV IT IS MEANINGLESS: we cannot move a $500M ADV name any more than we can move a $250M one, and fractional shares mean price per share is not a barrier either. It is an inherited large-fund ceiling sitting in a config, and it currently EXCLUDES the most liquid names in the market. THE WORK: raise or remove the upper bound so the universe opens, and keep the LOWER bound - it is doing real work by excluding names we genuinely could not trade. Report the new count and the new ADV distribution. Whatever you change must be a VERSIONED change with a written reason, because a universe definition is what every future study is computed against. WHAT THIS BUYS, AND BE HONEST ABOUT IT IN YOUR REPORT: it buys EVENT COUNT, not independence. The mechanism measured today that long-only mean pairwise correlation is 0.2811 and caps the universe at ~3.6 independent bets - and adding mega-caps to a US equity universe does not lower that, because they are MORE correlated with the index, not less. So do not report the wider universe as a breadth win on the independence axis. What it genuinely buys is more OCCURRENCES for the count-scaling event families - entry 8 post-filing drift, entry 12 dated catalysts, entry 14 placement discounts - which is exactly what the analyst is extracting a corpus for right now, and a 10x wider universe is roughly 10x the events. THE COUNTERWEIGHT TO STATE, because someone chose that band for a reason: the original premise was plausibly to find NEGLECTED names. Opening to mega-caps means competing with everyone on the most-covered securities in the world. That is a real trade and the answer is probably that the EVENT families do not care - an 8-K is an 8-K - while any coverage-based or attention-based signal does. Say which of our menu entries the wider universe helps and which it hurts. NOT IN SCOPE: adding asset classes. The FX study came back measured-and-not-resolvable at our power, and adding asset classes before the gate can judge the one we have gives us four seats blocked by the same instrument.",
