  "AMENDS 0ffa4aee / 1b1fe08e - THREE MODES NAMED, AND THE alpaca-paper SYNC DIRECTION. CEO instructions 2026-08-21, verbatim: \"lets have 1. test 2. alpaca-paper 3. alpaca-prod [this is for actual trading with real $$$]\" and \"agree and alpaca paper would sync to what I can see on my alpaca screen [if there is no strategy tracking it then its okay too] and mock is what we are experimenting.\" THE ENUM: test | alpaca-paper | alpaca-prod. Build ALL THREE into the enum now - a two-mode design encodes assumptions that break when the third arrives. WIRE TWO. THREE MODES, THREE STORES, and this is not negotiable: paper NAV and real NAV must never be foldable together. Which of these dollars are real is not a question that should be answered by a tag on a row. alpaca-prod IS STRUCTURALLY UNREACHABLE until named preconditions are met - CEO-agreed. Selecting it must require more than the toggle: a code-level gate plus a written precondition list. The preconditions, agreed: (1) every control has FIRED AT LEAST ONCE in alpaca-paper and been observed doing it - the envelope declining, the drawdown halt halting, the drift alarm alarming, which requires the alarm to exist first; (2) book and venue reconcile clean or the divergence is explained and fenced; (3) the sign-inverted exit trigger is fixed (34338ef6) - non-negotiable before anything can be short; (4) a kill switch that is WIRED AND TESTED, not registered; (5) N real informative fills in the cost model, since every backtest charges a cost assumption never validated against a real fill. THE SYNC DIRECTION, and this is the part that needs the most care: in alpaca-paper the fund book should MATCH what the CEO sees on his Alpaca screen, and positions with no strategy tracking them are ACCEPTABLE. BUT THE MECHANISM MUST NOT VIOLATE THE ONE NON-NEGOTIABLE THAT HAS NEVER BENT: \"NAV folds from the event log only; broker equity is a comparison, never the truth.\" These are reconcilable and the distinction is the whole design. DO NOT read broker equity as NAV. DO append RECONCILING EVENTS with a stated basis, so that the FOLD produces the matching answer and the history remains reconstructible. That is the same pattern the phantom-fill remediation used: preserve, annotate, correct by appending, never overwrite. TWO CONSEQUENCES TO SURFACE LOUDLY WHEN IT LANDS. (a) NAV WILL MOVE $127.55 FOR A NON-MARKET REASON - book 1885.74 against broker equity 2013.29. That is exactly the shape of a number changing for bookkeeping rather than performance, and the CLEAN FIELD RULE guard rails apply in full: the magnitude is MEASURED not estimated, the pre-sync value is PRESERVED beside the new one, a human decides on the approval channel, and the record says who, why and when. A NAV step of that size must be UNMISTAKABLY marked as a reconciliation and must never be readable as return. (b) ROUGHLY $1,166.52 BECOMES UNMANAGED BOOK - GLD 0.424471, INTC 1.608762, MSFT 0.340051, NVDA 0.749886, SOFI 9.188190, XLE 2.749912, all held at the broker, none owned by a strategy, NONE CARRYING AN EXIT RULE. The CEO has accepted that they exist unmanaged; the PM must be told they are now inside the book so exit coverage is reported honestly rather than silently omitting them. NOTE THIS SUPERSEDES the PM R18 fence-the-cohort recommendation: the CEO has chosen to RECONCILE the divergence rather than fence it. Record that as a decision, do not let the two coexist.",
