  "THE CONTRADICTION CHECKER - stop the CEO being the fund own consistency instrument. CEO instruction 2026-08-21, verbatim: \"I am thinking how we can automate most of the checking and figuring out; cause one me human running at claude speed is hard.\" THE DIAGNOSIS, from a full day of evidence rather than a theory. Six defects were caught by the CEO and missed by ten seats, and EVERY ONE was found by looking at a RENDERED SURFACE - not by reading code, not by querying an endpoint, which is what every seat does. The builder said the same of its own work: looking at the rendered page found two defects no diff review would have, the header reading 11 while the new chip read 6, eight pixels apart, both suites green. THE PATTERN THAT MAKES IT AUTOMATABLE: every one was a CONTRADICTION between two things the fund ALREADY KNEW. desk_load said 18 while zero of those rows needed the CEO. A row said status open while its own text said EXECUTED. The page fetched /fund/desk/archives/memo while no such route existed. seat_telemetry said analyst running_now true while the analyst run was recorded hours earlier. A ticket said delete PaperConnector while the code comment three lines above the ternary explained why weekends need it. NONE OF THAT IS MISSING DATA. It is INCONSISTENT data, and the fund holds both halves and never compares them. Catching a contradiction needs no judgement - it needs a list of pairs that should agree. THE MACHINERY ALREADY EXISTS AND IS BLIND: app/fund/judgement.py does exactly this for VALUES - registered against live, with drift detection and a due_for_review report. It covers nineteen constants and 17 of its 19 triggers are unevaluable. The pattern is right; the coverage is the gap. DO NOT BUILD A SECOND SYSTEM - extend that one from values to contradictions. STARTING INVARIANT LIST, all six drawn from today and all mechanically checkable: (1) desk_load.total equals what the CEO page renders as awaiting him - the adversary independently asked for exactly this, feed the SAME row to both sides and record the pair; (2) every URL the UI fetches resolves to a route the spine serves - a caller with no callee, which is how Donna memo card renders a permanent absence; (3) seat_telemetry.running_now agrees with the run log - a seat lit as working whose run is already recorded is a contradiction; (4) no recommendation sits at status open while its own text asserts it was executed; (5) book and venue reconcile, or the divergence is a named and accepted figure rather than a silent one; (6) every registered value equals the live code value - what judgement.py already does, extended past nineteen. OUTPUT ROUTING MATTERS AS MUCH AS DETECTION: this must reach the CEO desk RANKED, not a log. A checker whose output lands in a log nobody reads has moved the problem, not solved it - and this fund has four instruments that report absence as zero precisely because nothing read them. THE HONEST LIMIT, and state it in the docstring so nobody over-trusts the thing: A CONTRADICTION CHECKER CANNOT CATCH A DEFECT WHERE BOTH SOURCES ARE WRONG THE SAME WAY. The $652.09 figure was perfectly consistent - the spec said it, the chair repeated it three times, the code baked it into a permanent note. Nothing disagreed. Catching that needed a recompute from the per-leg table, which is the adversary discipline and stays a seat. Two different jobs: contradictions are automatable and should stop reaching the CEO at all; shared errors need an adversarial recompute and always will.",
