  "FUND MODE: mock | paper, one deliberate switch with a UI toggle - and the ledger question that decides whether it is safe. CEO instruction 2026-08-21, verbatim: \"Lets have mock mode for testing and paper mode where we actually deploy strategies and the UI needs to give a toggle so I can switch from mock mode where we are testing out things to trading mode where we have our live strategies. This would also be relevant when we run our stress tests against past market events in future.\" SUPERSEDES d8f2a2ff and 5cdb161b - implement this instead; they described the defect, this describes the fix. WHY THIS IS THE RIGHT SHAPE: we do not lack a switch, we have THREE accidental ones - USE_FAKE_FIRESTORE, FUND_REAL_BROKER, and the mere PRESENCE of ALPACA_API_KEY - scattered across a nested ternary at fund.py:151-163, two of whose branches reach a simulator silently. The CEO is replacing three implicit switches with one explicit one. THE DESIGN HAS TWO DIMENSIONS, NOT ONE, AND CONFLATING THEM IS THE ORIGINAL SIN: a mode is (WHERE ORDERS GO) x (WHERE EVENTS LAND). Today those are tangled through a single flag named for the ledger, which is exactly how a durability fix silently re-routed order execution to a real broker. Make both explicit. mock = simulated fills at REAL prices (live_pricer) + an ISOLATED ledger. paper = real Alpaca paper account + the fund own ledger. replay (future, the CEO stress tests) = historical prices + an ISOLATED ledger. THE MEASUREMENT THAT DECIDES THE LEDGER QUESTION, and it is not close: the live event log ALREADY carries 73 venue-labelled events - 42 paper and 31 alpaca - IN ONE STORE, distinguished only by a self-declared string. We know that string lies: the CEO-authorised experimental deployment filled on the PAPER connector wearing an alpaca label and produced zero cost information. A toggle that writes MOCK fills into that same log is the phantom-fill class of defect with a switch on the front. RECOMMENDATION: mock writes to a SEPARATE STORE. krypton_fund_test already exists on the same Postgres instance. A fold bug that contaminates NAV is unrecoverable and the CLEAN FIELD RULE says fence what cannot be re-baselined - so do not rely on filtering a tag out of one stream. FIVE REQUIREMENTS. (1) THE TOGGLE IS A CONTROL, not a preference: switching modes changes where real money-shaped orders go. It must append an event naming who switched, when and to what; it must REFUSE while any order is pending or unresolved; and it must be the CEO click, not a chair action. (2) MODE IS STAMPED BY THE SPINE, NEVER DECLARED BY THE PROPOSER. exitrule.py:301 hardcodes venue=paper on every exit regardless of the executing connector - that is precisely why R19 reads connector.positions() and never order[venue]. Same lesson: derive the mode from the runtime, make it unforgeable. (3) A MOCK VENUE MUST BE INCAPABLE OF EMITTING AN ALPACA-LABELLED FILL. Not discouraged - incapable. (4) MODE TRAVELS WITH EVERY ARTIFACT: the fill, the event, the book, NAV, the TCA reader, and the UI. A mock NAV and a paper NAV are different numbers and must never be able to be confused. (5) THE UI MUST BE UNMISTAKABLE. Not a small switch in a corner - in mock mode the whole surface should say so, because the failure this prevents is a human reading a mock number as real. Honour the design system: hierarchy from type and space, emerald is the fund and violet is the machine. UNSET MUST FAIL. No default, no fallback: a fund that cannot determine its own mode must refuse to construct an order path at all. That is Part A of d8f2a2ff and it survives into this design. NOT IN SCOPE: the replay engine itself (market-closed queue f2d70a55) - but design the mode enum so replay slots in as a third member rather than a special case.",
